        "original_id": "5e41e4c0-291f-58ba-9092-4cb2ee447e08",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: Florida black bear, American black bear, Big Cypress fox squirrel, brown pelican, wood stork, bald eagle, red-cockaded woodpecker, American crocodile\n- Places: Florida, Alabama, Georgia, Mississippi, North America, Collier-Seminole State Park\n- Concepts: subspecies, habitat, range\n\nFacts:\n- The American black bear, Ursus americanus, is a medium-sized bear native to North America.\n- The Florida black bear, Ursus americanus floridanus, is a subspecies of the American black bear.\n- The Florida black bear has historically ranged throughout most of Florida and the southern portions of Alabama, Georgia, and Mississippi.\n- Collier-Seminole State Park is inhabited by brown pelicans, wood storks, bald eagles, red-cockaded woodpeckers, American crocodiles, Florida black bears, and Big Cypress fox squirrels.",
